    // From n=14: 286 = 294 + 14c + d â†’ 14c + d = -8
    // â†’ 2c = 0 â†’ c = 0, d = -8
    // Hmm, that gives E â‰ˆ (3/2)n^2 - 8
    // Let's check: n=4: 24-8=16 vs 20. No! 
    // Actually (3/2)*16 = 24. 20 vs 24-8=16. 20 > 16. OK.
